WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.367
-Welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:06.334
Ladies and gentlemen...
happy Friday.

00:00:06.334 --> 00:00:07.834
Happy Friday, everyone.

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:09.334
Let's get to some news here.

00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:11.400
Well, guys,
the Department of Defense

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.000
just made a pretty
shocking announcement.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.167
Watch this.

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:17.300
-The Pentagon now confirming
and investigating

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.667
this video of a UFO

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:22.300
captured by Navy ships
in California.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.834
The big questions now,

00:00:23.834 --> 00:00:26.767
what exactly is
that mysterious object,

00:00:26.767 --> 00:00:28.133
and where did it come from?

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.667
-Anyway, have a great weekend,
everybody.

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:31.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:33.634
♪♪

00:00:33.634 --> 00:00:34.634
Wow.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:39.901
Right now, there are only --
I mean, a UFO!

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:42.434
There are only two explanations
for a random flying object.

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:43.901
It is either aliens

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:45.934
or another gender reveal
that has gone way too far.

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:47.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:49.534
Can we see the UFO again, Alex?

00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:50.634
-Oh, my God.

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:52.234
-It looks like
a Totino's Pizza Roll

00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:55.200
making its way
through our system.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.634
I see it.

00:00:56.634 --> 00:00:59.767
It's either a UFO or a Dorito
at the bottom of a pool.

00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:02.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:05.133
Nice to see the Navy
spent their military budget

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:07.834
on Nokia flip-phone cameras.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:10.467
-Got it!
-Sure. It's a UFO.

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:11.834
Hey, this is exciting.

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:14.534
Today, President Biden had
his first in-person meeting

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:15.734
with a foreign leader,

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:17.701
hosting
the prime minister of Japan.

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:18.934
-Ooh.

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:20.968
-Yeah, when Biden started
telling him a story,

00:01:20.968 --> 00:01:23.801
the 12-hour flight
suddenly didn't seem so long.

00:01:23.801 --> 00:01:25.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:26.734
"I used to go to Japan,

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:30.667
and we used to cook the sushi
on an engine block."

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:34.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:35.400
What?

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.801
Yeah, a 12-hour flight to
discuss problems facing Japan.

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:41.367
Afterwards, the prime minister
was quoted as saying,

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:44.501
"This could have been a Zoom."

00:01:44.501 --> 00:01:45.634
Some business news.

00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:47.434
I read that Subway
has been struggling

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:48.934
and could be up for sale.

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:50.400
-Ooh.
-Yeah.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.767
For some reason,

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:54.367
peeling off sweaty cold cuts
like they're Post-it notes

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:56.200
and slapping them on sugar bread

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.167
isn't resonating
with customers anymore.

00:02:00.334 --> 00:02:01.968
It's hard to say
if Subway's struggles

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:03.934
are from increased competition,

00:02:03.934 --> 00:02:05.400
changing consumer patterns,

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:06.667
or maybe, I don't know,

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:09.400
their spokesman
being in prison for pedophilia.

00:02:10.601 --> 00:02:14.501
It could be -- Any of those
could be the problem.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.234
-Yeah, it's a pick 'em.
I don't know which one.

00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:17.601
-I knew something was wrong
with Subway

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:19.000
when I dropped my sandwich
the other day

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.467
and it bounced back on my plate.

00:02:20.467 --> 00:02:22.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.934
They go to switch things up
over there.

00:02:24.934 --> 00:02:26.501
Hey, if you're in the market
for a new car --

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:27.901
Anyone looking for a new car?

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:29.300
[ Cheers ]

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:33.200
Mercedes just unveiled
a $100,000 electric sedan,

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.133
and it does more than just
get from you A to B.

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:36.200
Watch this.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.267
-The new electric car
from Mercedes

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:42.701
has all kinds of high-tech
features, including a nap mode.

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:46.167
The seat automatically reclines
to a resting level.

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:48.200
The interior lighting
and temperature

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.701
adjust to soothing levels.

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:53.367
The stereo provides
relaxing sounds,

00:02:53.367 --> 00:02:56.634
and a starry night
appears on the dashboard.

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:58.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.634 --> 00:02:59.734
-Yeah.

00:02:59.734 --> 00:03:01.567
-That's the feature
I've been missing.

00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:02.968
"I'll be right back, honey.

00:03:02.968 --> 00:03:05.400
I'm just gonna go out for
a 70-mile-per-hour nap.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.033
Not to be outdone,
the new Hyundais

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:10.834
have a little holder thing
for a pen.

00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:12.167
-Ooh.

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:15.534
Class.
-Speaking of luxury,

00:03:15.534 --> 00:03:17.667
I saw that two unlikely brands
have teamed up

00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:20.033
to create some high-end
camping gear.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.200
Check this out.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.667
-Italian luxury label Gucci
is teaming up

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:26.634
with outdoor recreation company
The North Face

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:29.033
to take glamping
to a whole new level.

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:32.467
This tent is part of
the North Face Gucci collection.

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:37.133
The Gucci North Face tent
will cost you close to $3,500.

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:38.467
-Hmm.
-Yep.

00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:40.167
The Gucci camping tent
goes perfectly

00:03:40.167 --> 00:03:41.801
with your napping Mercedes.

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:43.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:44.801
-I was already thinking that.
-You were?

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:46.100
-Yeah.
-You should check it out.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:49.033
This is nice -- The tent also
comes with dry $20 bills

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:50.234
that you can use as kindling.

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:51.234
-Oh!

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:53.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:56.100
"Throw another hundy
in the fire, hon.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.901
I'm gonna go back
in the mansion."

00:03:57.901 --> 00:03:59.434
The Gucci tent is kind of weird.

00:03:59.434 --> 00:04:01.400
It's like being asked on the red
carpet, "Who are you wearing?"

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.501
You're like,
"Dick's Sporting Goods."

00:04:03.501 --> 00:04:05.868
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:05.868 --> 00:04:07.267
What do you think of that?

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:09.033
-Check, please.

00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:10.734
-Some more business news.

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:14.634
Miller Lite -- Miller Lite
is selling one-sleeve t-shirts

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:16.334
for people to wear
when they get the vaccine.

00:04:16.334 --> 00:04:17.701
Take a look at this.

00:04:17.701 --> 00:04:20.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.968
Yeah, a one-sleeve
Miller Lite t-shirt

00:04:21.968 --> 00:04:24.467
or as Walmart calls it,
"business casual."

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:26.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:28.100
If you can't figure out
how to roll up a sleeve,

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.434
I think you've already
had your Miller Time.

00:04:30.434 --> 00:04:32.033
It will be funny when you go
get the shot,

00:04:32.033 --> 00:04:34.300
and it's in the other arm.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:37.501
"The whole point of the shirt
is to --

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:41.100
I'll just wear it backwards."

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:42.567
Well, the fallout continues

00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:44.701
in the wake of
the Suez Canal blockage.

00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:46.767
There's now a shortage
of garden gnomes.

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:47.834
-Ugh.

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:49.067
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:49.067 --> 00:04:50.901
-Today, everyone working
at Travelocity

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:53.868
looked at their gnome
like he was a bitcoin.

00:04:53.868 --> 00:04:55.834
"We're rich!"

00:04:55.834 --> 00:04:56.968
This is interesting.

00:04:56.968 --> 00:04:58.667
In Siberia, a group
of volunteers

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:00.901
cleaned up trash around the city

00:05:00.901 --> 00:05:03.801
on the anniversary
of the first human space flight.

00:05:03.801 --> 00:05:05.701
And they did it in style.
Watch this.

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:10.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:16.033
Is it me, or are the Disney+
spinoffs losing quality?

00:05:16.033 --> 00:05:17.534
You get that?

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:20.167
If you're feeling like
you're having a bad day,

00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:21.634
just remember,
there's a guy in Siberia

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:24.300
picking up trash in
a homemade Chewbacca costume.

00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:27.968
And finally, a singer
in British Columbia

00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:30.100
just set the world record
for the lowest note

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.400
ever recorded by a woman.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:32.767
Listen to this.

00:05:32.767 --> 00:05:34.868
-[ Deep voice ] ♪ La, la ♪

00:05:34.868 --> 00:05:37.000
♪ La, la ♪

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:44.968
♪ La, la, laaaaaa ♪

00:05:44.968 --> 00:05:48.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.934 --> 00:05:50.133
-I think one more note,

00:05:50.133 --> 00:05:51.634
and her lunch would have made
an appearance.

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:56.834
That's actually bear for,
"Wow, is that tent Gucci?"

00:05:56.834 --> 00:05:58.534
Did you hear about this?
White Claw is coming out

00:05:58.534 --> 00:06:00.801
with a new drink
called "White Claw Surge."

00:06:00.801 --> 00:06:03.234
-[ Laughing ] Yeah,
I've heard about that.

00:06:03.234 --> 00:06:05.501
-It comes in a bigger
can than regular White Claw,

00:06:05.501 --> 00:06:07.133
and it has almost
double the alcohol.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:08.634
[ Cheers ]

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.601
It's gonna be a hit.
-Has twice as much alcohol.

00:06:10.601 --> 00:06:12.601
-Yeah, it's gonna be
a big hit this summer.

00:06:12.601 --> 00:06:14.100
-Huge hit. Big smash.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.067
-People will be smashed, yes.

00:06:16.067 --> 00:06:17.801
I thought it would be helpful
to break down

00:06:17.801 --> 00:06:19.701
all of the differences
between regular White Claw

00:06:19.701 --> 00:06:20.767
and White Claw Surge.

00:06:20.767 --> 00:06:21.834
-Oh good.
-Help people out.

00:06:21.834 --> 00:06:23.434
First, White Claw...

00:06:26.367 --> 00:06:27.267
-Mm-hmm.

00:06:27.267 --> 00:06:28.801
-White Claw Surge...

00:06:31.334 --> 00:06:32.868
-Whoa. Okay, got it.

00:06:32.868 --> 00:06:34.167
-Also, White Claw...

00:06:35.834 --> 00:06:36.834
-Mm-hmm.

00:06:36.834 --> 00:06:37.834
-White Claw Surge...

00:06:39.767 --> 00:06:40.968
-Oh, that's good.

00:06:40.968 --> 00:06:43.100
[ Laughter ]
You choose.

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.200
-Next, White Claw...

00:06:46.434 --> 00:06:47.667
White Claw Surge...

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.234
"I'm just gonna do it
real quick!"

00:06:53.234 --> 00:06:54.400
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:56.567
-"The panda's
getting close to me. Uh-oh."

00:06:56.567 --> 00:06:57.934
-"He's mad."
-"He's mad.

00:06:57.934 --> 00:07:00.400
He doesn't like me being here."

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.200
-"And that's all I remember."

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:03.834
-[ Scoffs ] What are you doing?

00:07:03.834 --> 00:07:05.501
Here's another one.
White Claw's slogan is...

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:08.868
White Claw Surge's slogan is...

00:07:11.868 --> 00:07:14.667
[ Applause ]
That's bad.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:16.000
Next, White Claw...

00:07:17.968 --> 00:07:18.968
White Claw Surge...

00:07:20.801 --> 00:07:22.767
-You never know.

00:07:22.767 --> 00:07:23.734
Next up, White Claw...

00:07:25.667 --> 00:07:26.601
White Claw Surge...

00:07:29.734 --> 00:07:31.501
[ Applause ]

00:07:31.501 --> 00:07:32.667
And finally, White Claw...

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.467
White Claw Surge...

00:07:38.901 --> 00:07:40.467
There you go. Now you know.
-Now I know!

